    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "In my opinion the first issue is on CUDA's side, because the memory required to perform an SVD on tall matrices should be linear with respect to the input size, and here it is clearly quadratic. I posted about this in nvidia developer channel (https://devtalk.nvidia.com/default/topic/1057891/gpu-accelerated-libraries/cusolver-can-t-compute-svd-on-tall-matrices-with-cuda-10-1-buffersize-grows-quadratically/) but haven't got any answer yet.\r\n\r\nThe second issue is the integer overflow. If CUDA's `gesvd` actually requires a quadratic amount of memory, then for values above `2**31`, either we will get `CUSOLVER_STATUS_INVALID_VALUE` (overflow to negative), or we won't get the error but likely won't allocate enough memory (overflow to positive).",
    "created_at": "2019-08-06T15:58:24Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/cupy/cupy/issues/2351#issuecomment-518732932",
    "id": 518732932,
